(FIL-48: Read from standard input into <buffer> reads the process's stdin.
 This probe needs input on stdin; the recorded command supplies it.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Extended 2026-10-05 (files batch C): appended rendered shapes of
 'gen leaf standard input read'. The original lines read the whole input
 first, so the appended reads meet EOF - the bounds still hold. Run with
 the command below, not the original printf.
 Ran (vox 0.4.15, 2026-10-05): VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-48.vox -o p && printf 'hello world, this is the input\nsecond line\n' | ./p
 exit code 0; actual output:
   43
   hello world, this is the input
   second line
   
   1
   FIL-48 ok
   FIL-48 ok
   FIL-48 ok
   1
   FIL-48 ok
   FIL-48 ok
   FIL-48 ok
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
a buffer called bulk is 64 bytes in size.
Read from standard input into bulk.
print bulk's size.
print bulk.
a text called 'the workspace' is "vf_scratch/files/fil-48-c1".
Create a directory called 'the workspace'.
a buffer called 'storeroom' is 19 bytes in size.
a boolean called 'storeroom read flagged' is false.
Read from standard input into 'storeroom'.
On error Set 'storeroom read flagged' to true.
Print 'storeroom read flagged'.
If 'storeroom's size is greater than 43 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-48: expected at most 43 got {'storeroom's size}", Exit 95. Print "FIL-48 ok".
If 'storeroom's size is greater than 19 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-48: expected at most 19 got {'storeroom's size}", Exit 95. Print "FIL-48 ok".
a number called 'storeroom bytes taken from standard input' is 'storeroom's size.
If 'storeroom bytes taken from standard input' is greater than 43 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-48: expected at most 43 got {'storeroom bytes taken from standard input'}", Exit 95. Print "FIL-48 ok".
a text called 'the workspace' is "vf_scratch/files/fil-48-c2".
Create a directory called 'the workspace'.
a buffer called 'the tally sheet' is 14 bytes in size.
a boolean called 'the tally sheet read flagged' is false.
Read from standard input into 'the tally sheet'.
On error Set 'the tally sheet read flagged' to true.
Print 'the tally sheet read flagged'.
If 'the tally sheet's size is greater than 43 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-48: expected at most 43 got {'the tally sheet's size}", Exit 95. Print "FIL-48 ok".
If 'the tally sheet's size is greater than 14 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-48: expected at most 14 got {'the tally sheet's size}", Exit 95. Print "FIL-48 ok".
a number called 'the tally sheet bytes taken from standard input' is 'the tally sheet's size.
If 'the tally sheet bytes taken from standard input' is greater than 43 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-48: expected at most 43 got {'the tally sheet bytes taken from standard input'}", Exit 95. Print "FIL-48 ok".
